    "gen_ai.input.messages": "[{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"<session_context>\\nThis is the Gemini CLI. We are setting up the context for our chat.\\nToday's date is Thursday, October 15, 2026 (formatted according to the user's locale).\\nMy operating system is: darwin\\nThe project's temporary directory is: /Users/mohammadpoorahmadi/.gemini/tmp/run\\n- **Workspace Directories:**\\n  - /Users/mohammadpoorahmadi/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/assignments/03-anatomy-of-coding-agents/gemini-cli-dissection/work/run\\n- **Directory Structure:**\\n\\nShowing up to 200 items (files + folders). Folders or files indicated with ... contain more items not shown, were ignored, or the display limit (200 items) was reached.\\n\\n/Users/mohammadpoorahmadi/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/assignments/03-anatomy-of-coding-agents/gemini-cli-dissection/work/run/\\n├───.DS_Store\\n├───.gitignore\\n├───GEMINI.md\\n├───README.md\\n├───requirements.txt\\n├───TASK.md\\n├───.gemini/\\n│   └───settings.json\\n├───.pytest_cache/...\\n├───shopcart/\\n│   ├───__init__.py\\n│   ├───cart.py\\n│   ├───catalog.py\\n│   ├───pricing.py\\n│   └───__pycache__/...\\n└───tests/\\n    ├───__init__.py\\n    ├───test_cart.py\\n    ├───test_pricing.py\\n    └───__pycache__/...\\n\\n\\n<loaded_context>\\n<project_context>\\n--- Context from: /Users/mohammadpoorahmadi/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/assignments/03-anatomy-of-coding-agents/gemini-cli-dissection/work/run/GEMINI.md ---\\n# Project context\\n\\n- Python 3.10+ library; no third-party runtime dependencies.\\n- All money is integer **cents**. Never use floats for stored amounts.\\n- Run tests with `python -m pytest -q` from the repository root.\\n- Keep functions small; pricing rules live in `shopcart/pricing.py`, cart state in `shopcart/cart.py`.\\n--- End of Context from: /Users/mohammadpoorahmadi/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/assignments/03-anatomy-of-coding-agents/gemini-cli-dissection/work/run/GEMINI.md ---\\n</project_context>\\n</loaded_context>\\n</session_context>\"},{\"text\":\"Read TASK.md and complete all of it. First write out your plan, then carry it out without waiting for my confirmation.\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"functionCall\":{\"name\":\"update_topic\",\"args\":{\"title\":\"Reading TASK.md and Planning\",\"strategic_intent\":\"Reading TASK.md to understand the assignment requirements and formulating a comprehensive plan to complete all tasks.\"},\"id\":\"call_365612\"},\"thoughtSignature\":\"\"},{\"functionCall\":{\"name\":\"read_file\",\"args\":{\"file_path\":\"TASK.md\"},\"id\":\"call_365613\"}}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"functionResponse\":{\"id\":\"call_365612\",\"name\":\"update_topic\",\"response\":{\"output\":\"Current topic: \\\"Reading TASK.md and Planning\\\"\\nTopic summary: ...\\n\\nStrategic Intent: Reading TASK.md to understand the assignment requirements and formulating a comprehensive plan to complete all tasks.\"}}},{\"functionResponse\":{\"id\":\"call_365613\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"response\":{\"output\":\"# Task\\n\\n## 1. Fix the failing tests\\n`python -m pytest` currently fails. Make the whole suite pass by fixing the code in\\n`shopcart/`. The existing tests describe the intended behavior — do not edit them for\\nthis step.\\n\\n## 2. Add shipping to cart totals\\n- Orders pay a flat **$5.99** shipping fee (`599` cents).\\n- Shipping is **free** when the subtotal *after discount, before tax* is **$50.00 or more**.\\n- An empty cart pays no shipping.\\n- Shipping is **not taxed**: `total = tax(discounted subtotal) + shipping`.\\n- Put the shipping rule in `shopcart/pricing.py` and use it from `Cart.total()`.\\n\\nSome existing tests check `Cart.total()` with values from before shipping existed. You may\\nupdate those expected values — and only those — and note why in a comment.\\n\\n## 3. Test it\\nAdd tests covering the shipping rules (including the free-shipping threshold), then run\\nthe full suite and confirm it passes.\\n\"}}}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"functionCall\":{\"name\":\"run_shell_command\",\"args\":{\"command\":\"python -m pytest\",\"description\":\"Run pytest to check current test failures\"},\"id\":\"call_318944\"},\"thoughtSignature\":\"\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"functionResponse\":{\"id\":\"call_318944\",\"name\":\"run_shell_command\",\"response\":{\"output\":\"<untrusted_context>\\nOutput: ====================================================================================== test session starts =======================================================================================\\nplatform darwin -- Python 3.13.13, pytest-9.1.1, pluggy-1.7.0\\nrootdir: /Users/mohammadpoorahmadi/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/assignments/03-anatomy-of-coding-agents/gemini-cli-dissection/work/run\\ncollected 14 items                                                                                                                                                                               \\n\\ntests/test_cart.py ..F.....F                                                                                                                                                               [ 64%]\\ntests/test_pricing.py .....                                                                                                                                                                [100%]\\n\\n============================================================================================ FAILURES ============================================================================================\\n__________________________________________________________________________ test_add_same_item_twice_increments_quantity __________________________________________________________________________\\n\\n    def test_add_same_item_twice_increments_quantity():\\n        cart = Cart()\\n        cart.add_item(\\\"MUG\\\")\\n        cart.add_item(\\\"MUG\\\", 2)\\n>       assert cart.items == {\\\"MUG\\\": 3}\\nE       AssertionError: assert {'MUG': 2} == {'MUG': 3}\\nE         \\nE         Differing items:\\nE         {'MUG': 2} != {'MUG': 3}\\nE         Use -v to get more diff\\n\\ntests/test_cart.py:21: AssertionError\\n_____________________________________________________________________________ test_fixed_discount_applied_before_tax _____________________________________________________________________________\\n\\n    def test_fixed_discount_applied_before_tax():\\n        cart = Cart()\\n        cart.add_item(\\\"TEE\\\")\\n        cart.add_item(\\\"TEE\\\")\\n        cart.apply_code(\\\"TENOFF\\\")\\n>       assert cart.total() == 3240  # (4000 - 1000) + 8% tax\\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\nE       assert 1160 == 3240\\nE        +  where 1160 = total()\\nE        +    where total = <shopcart.cart.Cart object at 0x101f6f750>.total\\n\\ntests/test_cart.py:61: AssertionError\\n==================================================================================== short test summary info ===========================...[TRUNCATED: original length 74256]",
